  "summary": "A Washington state trial court ruled that data captured by Flock Safety ALPR cameras used by Stanwood and Sedro-Woolley are public records under the state's Public Records Act, rejecting the cities' arguments that data stored on Flock's servers fell outside disclosure rules. The cities had shut off their Flock cameras during the litigation, and the requester ultimately could not obtain the footage because it had been auto-deleted.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The Flock images generated by the Flock cameras...are public records",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "data generated by Flock [automated license plate reader cameras (ALPRs)] and stored in the Flock cloud system are not public records unless and until a public agency extracts and downloads that data.",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    },
    {
      "quote": "The cities both allowed the records to be automatically deleted after I submitted my records requests and while they decided to have their legal council review my request.",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    }
  ],
